<section class="meaning section-line">
  <div class="narrow center">
    <div class="eyebrow">What is the 490 Life?</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">The end of counting.</h2>
    <div class="meaning" style="text-align:left">
      <p><strong>The question.</strong> Peter thought he was being generous: &ldquo;Lord, how often shall my brother sin against me and I forgive him? Up to seven times?&rdquo; Seven was more than double what the rabbis required. He was ready to be congratulated.</p>
      <p><strong>The answer.</strong> Jesus said, &ldquo;I do not say to you up to seven times, but up to seventy times seven.&rdquo; Four hundred ninety. Not a higher ceiling &mdash; the end of ceilings. Nobody keeping count gets to 490. That's the point: the people of a forgiving God stop counting.</p>
      <p><strong>The invitation.</strong> The 490 Life is life shaped by that answer &mdash; receiving a forgiveness you could never earn, and learning to give it away. This site is a place to walk that road: teachings from Scripture every week, honest resources, and a book that traces grace from the heart of God to the wounded places of ordinary life.</p>
    </div>
    <hr class="gold-rule">
  </div>
</section>

